    "transcript": "This straw isn't broken, so why does it snap at the water's surface? Light from the straw speeds up as it leaves the water and changes direction. Like a mower rolling from grass to pavement, one side speeds up first. Your brain traces the light back in a straight line, so the underwater part looks higher. That's why a pool looks shallower from above, about three-quarters of its real depth. Download Recall to turn your study material into lessons.",
